I have not seen this mentioned before, although I must
confess that I have not read every line of every post
ever posted, much less even read all of the spoiler files.  
If this is a well known trick, then I apologize.

You read an identify scroll, and if it is blessed, it will
identify as much as you ask it to.  So, suppose ya got a
ring that you *really* want identified, but also a spellbook
or two, and then other crap that it'd be nice to know curse status
of.  But the main thing is the ring.

Did you know you can answer
     Which sorts of things would you like identified[)[("+= a]?
with more than one argument?  So e.g. if we do

Which sorts of things would you like identified[)[("+= a]?   =+()["

it will first do your ring(s), then if it can continue, it will
continue onto the spellbooks, then the tools, etc...

What a friggin waste of blessed scrolls I've been!  Never thought
to pass two or more arguments to an identify scroll of unknown
curse status.  Do it in the right order so you at least get what
ya need, and life is good.

(You can also pass multiple arguments to any of the "Which sorts..."
questions, e.g. to Drop stuff).
